Subject: `fill` scale of `geom_point` is not shown in the legend
Message-ID: <2ZdLWHN5xFY.hr46MvhSZPYJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/2ZdLWHN5xFY/m/hr46MvhSZPYJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

 <http://i.stack.imgur.com/O3aIC.png>
My sample code is as following:
set.seed(1)
df <- data.frame(xx=sample(10,6), yy=sample(10,6),
                 type2=c('a','b','a','a','b','b'),
                 type3=c('A','C','B','A','B','C') )
ggplot(data=df, mapping = aes(x=xx, y=yy)) +
  geom_point(aes(shape=type3, fill=type2), size=5) +
  scale_shape_manual(values=c(24,25,21)) +
  scale_fill_manual( values=c('green', 'red'))

Resulting plot has a legend but it's 'type2' section doesn't reflect scale of fill value.
I asked on Stackoverflow and was suggested a workaround <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/27221011/> which works by drawing one more layer of points, but I still don't understand why the scale is not shown natively, so I would really appreciate authors' comments.

