Message-ID: <2ZdLWHN5xFY.1Dvxn_g_r7oJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <2ZdLWHN5xFY.hr46MvhSZPYJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <2ZdLWHN5xFY.hr46MvhSZPYJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/2ZdLWHN5xFY/m/1Dvxn_g_r7oJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The geom used in the legend is a solid point, so it doesn't have a fill. You can force it to use another symbol, like this:

ggplot(data=df, mapping = aes(x=xx, y=yy)) +
  geom_point(aes(shape=type3, fill=type2), size=5) +
  scale_shape_manual(values=c(24,25,21)) +

  scale_fill_manual( values=c('green', 'red')) +
  guides(fill = guide_legend(override.aes = list(shape = 21)))

Best,
Ista

