Just tried this and I think you must mean yday?

> I would like the x-axis labels to display months rather than yearday, and I can't seem to find a straightforward way to do this.

Is there a requirement for your data to be yearday rather than an actual date?

# Create some data
df <- data.frame(
  date = seq(as.Date("2014-01-01"), len=365, by="1 day")[sample(365, 50)],
  value = runif(50)
)

# If it can be date:
ggplot(df,aes(x=date,y=value))+geom_point()+scale_x_date(labels=date_format("%b"),breaks=date_breaks("1 month"))

# if it needs to be yearday:
ggplot(df,aes(x=yday(date),y=value))+geom_point()+
  scale_x_continuous(breaks=sapply(1:12,function(x){yday(as.Date(paste("2014",x,"01",sep="-")))}),
  labels=sapply(1:12,function(x){month(as.Date(paste("2014",x,"01",sep="-")),label=TRUE,abbr=TRUE)}))

Regards,
Ron.

